The '''Skade national football team''' represents [[Skade]] in men's international association football. It is governed by the [[Skade Football Association]] and competes as a member of the Illypnian Football Confederation within the [[AFA]] confederation.

Skade are currently ranked 19th in the [[AFA Men's World Ranking]] and qualified for their sixth [[AFA World Cup]] at the [[2022 AFA World Cup|2022 tournament]].

== History ==

=== Early development ===
Skade's football tradition is rooted in the broader Illypnian sporting culture, with the domestic league producing technically disciplined players known for organised defending and set-piece proficiency. The Skade Premier League, established in 1972, is one of the older leagues in the region.

=== World Cup history ===
Skade first qualified for the World Cup in 1998 and have been regular qualifiers since. Their best result came in 2010, when a disciplined defensive display carried them to the quarter-finals before elimination. The 2022 tournament marks their sixth appearance.

